---
import TrustPageLayout from '../layouts/TrustPageLayout.astro';
import { AMAZON_LABEL, MARKET_LABEL, MARKET_PLAYERS, SITE_EMAIL, SITE_NAME } from '../lib/site';
---

<TrustPageLayout
	title={`About ${SITE_NAME}`}
	description={`How we research ${MARKET_LABEL} pickleball gear — catalog-backed guides, ${AMAZON_LABEL} availability, and clear buying advice.`}
	canonicalPath="/about"
>
	<p>
		{SITE_NAME} exists because buying pickleball gear online is noisy. Spec sheets contradict each other,
		“best of” lists blur into each other, and {MARKET_PLAYERS} often need clear {AMAZON_LABEL} availability
		without guessing whether a paddle, shoe, or net is even the right tool for the job.
	</p>
	<p>
		We publish practical, original guides for everyone who plays: beginners buying a first paddle, intermediates
		chasing spin, players protecting their joints, seniors prioritizing comfort, and competitive players refining
		a tournament bag. The goal is simple — help you spend once, on the right category of gear, with honest
		language about what we know and what we do not.
	</p>

	<h2>How the site works</h2>
	<p>
		Every product we feature in buying guides must exist in our curated catalog
		(<code>gear.json</code>). Articles reference products by ID; they do not invent parallel product databases
		with conflicting weights, materials, or links. That keeps affiliate URLs, images, and approximate price tiers
		in one place — and makes it obvious when something is missing.
	</p>
	<p>
		Guides live under <a href="/guides/how-to-choose-a-pickleball-paddle">/guides</a>, category pages under
		<a href="/gear/paddles">/gear</a>, and timely industry notes under <a href="/news">/news</a>. Category pages
		(paddles, shoes, nets) are the shopping surfaces; long-form guides explain <em>why</em> a shortlist fits a
		playing job. News posts summarize brand and tour developments with dated, attributed language — not invented
		quotes or unverified stats.
	</p>

	<h2>What our reviews are (and are not)</h2>
	<p>
		We write <strong>catalog-backed buying advice</strong>: we map products to real jobs (control, power, wide feet,
		portable courts), compare construction patterns that manufacturers publicly claim, and say who a pick is for.
		We do <strong>not</strong> pretend to run an independent lab, publish fabricated swing-weight numbers, invent
		star ratings, or claim “tested for 200 hours on court” credentials we do not have.
	</p>
	<ul>
		<li>We prioritize clarity over hype — including when a cheaper option is the smarter buy.</li>
		<li>
			We cross-check rules and court dimensions against
			<a href="https://usapickleball.org/" rel="noopener noreferrer">USA Pickleball</a>
			resources when a guide depends on regulation standards.
		</li>
		<li>
			When we cannot verify a claim from the manufacturer listing or our catalog notes, we mark it
			(<code>{'{{ TODO: confirm }}'}</code>) or omit it instead of guessing.
		</li>
		<li>
			Approximate price tiers ($, $$, $$$) and “as of” context may appear for orientation. They are never live
			store prices. Always confirm current pricing and availability on {AMAZON_LABEL}.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Who writes this</h2>
	<p>
		Guides and news updates are written and edited by
		<a href="/authors/deco">Deco</a> (Declan Martin), founder of {SITE_NAME}. Deco builds
		catalog-backed comparisons for paddles, court shoes, balls, bags, apparel, accessories, and portable nets for
		{MARKET_LABEL} shoppers. His focus is clear product criteria, practical buying frameworks, and honest
		disclosures — not hype, and not invented on-court credentials.
	</p>
	<p>
		If you want the full standards document — research process, correction policy, update cadence, and how
		affiliate relationships are walled off from rankings — read the
		<a href="/editorial-policy">editorial policy</a>. For commission and FTC language on every affiliate page, see
		the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure">affiliate disclosure</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>Independence and money</h2>
	<p>
		Product links may earn a commission through affiliate programs (primarily {AMAZON_LABEL}, plus optional brand
		or specialty retailers when configured). That never changes what we recommend or the price you pay. Rankings
		and shortlists are driven by playing job and catalog fit, not by which partner pays the highest rate. We do
		not accept payment for placements in editorial lists.
	</p>

	<h2>What we hope you get from us</h2>
	<p>
		A quieter decision. Fewer impulse buys driven by tour logos. A paddle, shoe, or net that matches how you
		actually play — beginner, improver, or tournament weekend warrior. When something on the site is wrong or
		outdated, tell us. Corrections and meaningful guide updates are part of the job, not an afterthought.
	</p>
	<p>
		Questions or corrections? Email
		<a href={`mailto:${SITE_EMAIL}`}>{SITE_EMAIL}</a>
		or use the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
	</p>
</TrustPageLayout>
